      "writtenOn": "2026-06-25T22:39:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Curious about what this warning was because we\u0027ve been moving toward `inline constexpr` instead of `static constexpr` as it usually saves binary size. https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/292135\n\nJust wondering why it triggered on this one file and not any of the other `inline constexpr`s.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "d351d3ce940066172caaf96c68c9b84a29d0818e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e01146c1_4f5cd00a",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/opengl/DisplayEGL.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000685
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-26T00:38:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For this one because it\u0027s a pointer. Just reverting this one should be trivial to binary size.\n\nThe other ones are pure values so they have no impact.\n\n(gemini\u0027s explain and I took it)\n\u003e Clang warns because if some code relies on the address of kNoConfig being the same everywhere, that code will break. For a pointer type like void*, Clang assumes the address identity might matter.",
      "parentUuid": "26965eed_d1757644",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "d351d3ce940066172caaf96c68c9b84a29d0818e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
